#. type: Title =
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tomb Kings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Attribute :dragon:
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zombie Dragon"
msgstr ""

#.  TODO: Logo is half the resolution of all the others.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:20
msgid ""
"image:tomb-kings/logo.webp[width=93,height=117,float=\"right\"] In ages past "
"the land of Khemri was fertile, populous and prosperous thanks to the waters "
"of the Great River of Life whose annual floods irrigated the fields and "
"guaranteed a bountiful harvest. Each city was ruled by a Priest King and for "
"many centuries these omnipotent monarchs lived and died and were buried in "
"tombs constructed by their faithful Liche Priests. The bodies of the Priest "
"Kings, and those of their most faithful troops and retainers, were carefully "
"embalmed and interred with holy spells of immortality to prepare them for "
"the far off day of re-awakening."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Unfortunately for the Priest Kings of Khemri their dreams of eternal life "
"were to be realised only in the most horrific way.  A rebellious Liche "
"Priest called Nagash overthrew the cities of Khemri and made himself ruler "
"of the entire land. Consequently he was driven into exile and eventually "
"murdered. However, this was not the end of Nagash, for he was the greatest "
"Sorcerer of his day if not all of all time, and whilst the Black Pyramid "
"endured Nagash’s spirit could always find refuge there. His evil was "
"gradually absorbed into the Black Pyramid and his body reborn in the "
"sorcerous sarcophagus that lay deep within."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Nagash’s vengeance upon his enemies was absolute. From deep within the Black "
"Pyramid he worked upon a great spell of death that he eventually cast upon "
"the whole land of Khemri.  Consequently a pestilence fell upon the nation "
"and all living things sickened and died so that soon there were none to bury "
"the dead and the cities became nothing but empty tombs. What was alive was "
"now dead, and what was dead was revivified as undead. On that terrible day "
"the rulers of old awoke to the horror that had befallen them. The golden "
"immortality in which they had believed had proven a false dream. The Tomb "
"Kings were mightily angered to discover that they had been treated in this "
"way – and there were a great many of them. Whole dynasties rose as one, "
"ancient rivals and bitter enemies side by side. But most of all their anger "
"was reserved for Nagash. They saw the Black Pyramid and felt the dark winds "
"of sorcery that blew about its shining black walls and understood that they "
"had been betrayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:64
msgid ""
"From their tombs the Tomb Kings have re-ordered their kingdoms. Their "
"peoples, mostly interred without the benefit of royal magic, are little more "
"than automatons. Undead armies wheel and manoeuvre with ingrained military "
"instinct, continually re-fighting old wars or pursuing new ones amidst the "
"dry deserts. The terrible spell that created them binds them to their land "
"but offers no succour. Those that perish in battle rise each dawn whilst "
"even those that are destroyed entirely, burned to smoke or vaporised by "
"sorcery, live on as spiteful spirits that can be heard in the wailing of the "
"wind and groaning of great stones in the mountains. If the Tomb Kings take "
"any comfort it is only in the recreation of their ancient empires – a shadow "
"of former existence that evokes memories of the lives that they once led."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tomb kings army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$tomb-kings.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:81
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "Undead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:84
msgid ""
"Undead units never act on initiative. An Undead unit only moves in the "
"Command phase if given orders (except Carrion who can also home back as "
"noted below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:87
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:93
msgid ""
"Undead units are unaffected by the −1 Command penalty for enemy within 20cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:90
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:96
msgid ""
"Undead units are unaffected by the −1 Combat penalty for fighting terrifying "
"troops."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:93
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:99
msgid ""
"Undead units are unaffected by the Confusion rule – they cannot become "
"confused for any reason."
msgstr ""

#. 6: Space before +1
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[carrion,†1]]1. Carrion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:104
msgid ""
"Carrion can fly. Note that Carrion can always return to a character by "
"homing back at the start of the Command phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bone-giant,†2]]2. Bone Giant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:109
msgid ""
"Bone Giants cause terror. When a Tomb King gives an order to a Bone Giant or "
"a brigade that contains a Bone Giant there is a −1 Command penalty. There is "
"no penalty when a Liche-Priest gives an order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[sphinx,†3]]3. Sphinx"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:119
msgid ""
"Because the Sphinx has so many hits (6) we must consider the possibility of "
"hurting the Sphinx and reducing its effectiveness in subsequent turns. "
"Therefore, if a Sphinx has accumulated 4–5 hits by the end of the Shooting "
"phase or Combat phase and is no longer engaged in combat it is deemed to "
"have been badly hurt. Once a Sphinx is badly hurt all accumulated hits are "
"discounted and its maximum Hits and Attacks are halved for the rest of the "
"battle (to 3 Hits and 2 Attacks). The Sphinx causes terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[skull-chukka,†4]]4. Skull Chukka"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:129
msgid ""
"The Skull Chukka is a xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#stone-"
"thrower[Stone Thrower] but with the following additional rule.  When a unit "
"is driven back as a result of hits scored by a Skull Chukka, then any dice "
"rolled in respect to those hits will cause Confusion on the roll of 4, 5 or "
"6 (rather than 6 as normal). Note that if a unit has taken other hits as "
"well it will be necessary to roll the Skull Chukka dice separately. See the "
"Artillery and Machines section of the rulebook for the Stone Thrower rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:130
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bone-thrower,†5]]5. Bone Thrower"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:132
msgid ""
"The Bone Thrower is a xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#bolt-"
"thrower[Bolt Thrower] as described in the Rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:133
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[tomb-king,†6]]6. Tomb King"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:138
msgid ""
"The Tomb King is empowered by the spells cast upon him when buried. He can "
"use this power to increase the Combat Attacks value of all the stands in one "
"unit within 20cm by +1 for the duration of one Combat phase. This ability "
"can only be used once per battle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[zombie-dragon,†7]]7. Zombie Dragon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:141
msgid "A Tomb King or Liche Priest may ride a Zombie Dragon."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:144
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[liche-chariot,†8]]8. Liche Chariot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:146
msgid ""
"A Tomb King or Liche Priest can ride a chariot.  A character riding a "
"chariot adds +1 to his Attacks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tomb King spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:153
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:146
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raise Dead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:159
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:152
msgid ""
"_At the Wizard’s beckoning the mangled corpses that litter the battleground "
"rise from the dead to continue the slaughter._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:170
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:163
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast upon a combat engagement taking place within 30cm of "
"the Wizard. The spell can be cast regardless of whether the Wizard can see "
"any units in the combat engagement or not. A single combat engagement can "
"only be affected once by this spell in any turn regardless of how many units "
"are involved in the combat. For purposes of deciding whether a combat is "
"eligible as a target, combat engagements are as they appear when the die to "
"cast the spell is rolled: so it is possible for pursuit or advances to bring "
"two units of raised dead into the same engagement later on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:184
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:177
msgid ""
"A Skeleton unit of three stands is created. Each stand in the raised unit "
"must be placed so that its front edge contacts an enemy stand from the "
"targeted engagement, or that it supports a friendly stand from the same "
"engagement, including raised stands. The placement of stands may not split "
"up the engagement into multiple smaller engagements. If raised stands come "
"into contact with unengaged enemy units, those units will join the "
"engagement after the raised unit is placed, similar to incidental contact "
"during pursuit. If it is impossible to position all stands in combat or "
"support then the unit is not deployed and the spell fails. Raised dead do "
"not count as charging in the first round of combat. Raised dead are ignored "
"for working out break point and victory points at the end of the game."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:186
#, no-wrap
msgid "Touch of Death"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:192
msgid ""
"_The Wizard’s enemies crumble to dust as he smites them with the corrupting "
"Touch of Death._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:196
msgid ""
"The Wizard can cast this spell if he has joined a unit in combat.  The spell "
"can be cast on any single enemy unit that it is touching the unit the Wizard "
"has joined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:201
msgid ""
"The target unit takes three attacks worked out in the usual way.  Any hits "
"scored are carried over into the first round of combat and count as having "
"been struck in the first round for purposes of working out combat results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "Doom and Despair"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:209
msgid ""
"_A dark cloud of doom and despair settles over the enemy, sapping their "
"courage and dampening their warlike spirit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:221
msgid ""
"Whilst the spell lasts the unit cannot charge and if engaged in combat will "
"not pursue or advance. Even units that are otherwise obliged to charge, "
"pursue, or advance will not do so if affected by Doom and Despair. Note that "
"even other Undead are not immune – they are overcome by the ennui of the "
"tomb!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:223
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:197
#, no-wrap
msgid "Death Bolt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:229
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:203
msgid ""
"_A fearsome bolt of sorcerous lightning flies from the Wizard’s outstretched "
"finger tips and strikes an enemy unit._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/tomb-kings.adoc:238
msgid ""
"The Death Bolt is treated like three ordinary shooting attacks except that "
"armour has no effect (all targets count as having no armour). A unit can be "
"driven back by a Death Bolt as with ordinary shooting."
msgstr ""
